# Two scoped lines, deliberately. See story c2-2 AC 5.
#
# src/companion/app/static/ is the committed SPA build output (AD-13). CI rebuilds it and
# compares the result against the committed bytes, so those bytes must not depend on which
# machine wrote them — and core.autocrlf is `true` on the maintainer's Windows box. `-text`
# settles that by declaration rather than by an argument about when git normalises: no eol
# conversion in either direction, on any platform.
#
# Three things this file deliberately is NOT:
#
#   * it is not `* text=auto`. A repo-wide pattern would renormalise every tracked file in the
#     repository, which is why c2-1 declined to create this file at all. A single path-scoped
#     pattern touches nothing outside that path.
#   * it is not `text eol=lf`. Story c2-5 self-hosts Space Grotesk .woff2 fonts into this same
#     directory, and an eol attribute on a binary font corrupts it.
#   * it is not inside src/companion/app/static/. Vite's emptyOutDir skip list is exactly
#     [".git"], so any file placed there is deleted by the next build.
src/companion/app/static/** -text

# The plugin mirror of the same bundle, and it needs the identical treatment for the identical
# reason — it is compared byte-for-byte against the source of truth (by the plugin/ drift check
# in CI, and by tests/unit/companion/test_spa.py::TestThePluginMirror).
#
# AC 5 called for one line; this second one is a deviation taken deliberately, because one line
# is measurably not enough. Measured on this machine: with only the src/ rule, a fresh clone
# under core.autocrlf=true writes src/.../index.html at 1093 bytes (LF, attribute honoured) and
# plugin/.../index.html at 1119 bytes (CRLF, no attribute) — 26 line endings apart, so the
# byte-identity test fails and the plugin drift check reports drift on an untouched tree. CI is
# ubuntu, where autocrlf is off, so CI could never have caught it: the failure is Windows-only
# and fresh-clone-only.
#
# This is still path-scoped. AC 5's actual concern — that a repo-wide pattern would renormalise
# every tracked file, which is why c2-1 declined to create this file — is untouched.
plugin/server/src/companion/app/static/** -text
